          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em
              Rational
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
            is the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+spectra"} equivariant spectra
            just on the level of their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable
            version of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %p
            A key general statement of the theory is that rationally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
            (even for non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalences
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+categories"} homotopy categories
            this was established by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"} John Greenlees
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zags"} zig-zags
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            this was established Greenlees and by his students,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Barnes"} David Barnes
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Magdalena+Kedziorek"} Magdalena Kedziorek
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#SplittingIntoMackeyFunctors Greenlees-May splitting into equivariant Eilenberg-MacLane spectra
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectrum"} G-spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(X) \in \mathcal{M}[G]
            for its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functor"} Mackey functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+groups"} equivariant homotopy groups
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Every rational
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is the direct sum of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectra"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectra
            (Mackey functors) on its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+groups"} equivariant homotopy groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E \simeq \prod_n \Sigma^n H\pi_n(E)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#GreenleesMay95"}> Greenlees-May 95, theorem A.1
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Greenlees"} Greenlees, theorem 5.1
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
            two
            = succeed "-spectra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi G
                  %mo ⟶
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [X,Y]_G \longrightarrow \underset{n}{\prod} Hom_{\mathcal{M}[G]}(\pi_n(X),\pi_n(Y))
                  \\,.
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is rational, then this is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            (
            %a{:href => "#GreenleesMay95"}> Greenlees-May 95, theorem A.4
            ).
